							{
								"box": {
									"code": "// codebox_seed.gen -- f_ks stage 0a: the reseed noise, a deterministic hash per texel. 256x256 float32.\n// Checked statistically (bench_ks.test_seed_noise_statistics); a seed only needs to be broadband and never constant.\n//\n// Inputs: the first inlet is the `r draw` bang (unused; it only triggers the render every frame).\n// Output: R = white noise in [0, 1). The pass stage reads it only on the frame reseed is 1.\n// `salt` changes the pattern: the patcher counts up on every reset, so each reset is a new random start.\n//   - no sin(): a Hoskins-style arithmetic hash (fract and multiply-add only), whose precision does not\n//     depend on the GPU's sin() range reduction\n//   - scalars only: components are never read from a stored vec\n//   - never name a variable e or phi (predefined constants)\nParam salt(0);\n\npx = floor(norm.x * 256) + salt * 61;\npy = floor(norm.y * 256) + salt * 17;\nha = fract(px * 0.1031);\nhb = fract(py * 0.1031);\nhc = ha;\nhd = ha * (hb + 33.33) + hb * (hc + 33.33) + hc * (ha + 33.33);\nha = ha + hd;\nhb = hb + hd;\nhc = hc + hd;\nhn = fract((ha + hb) * hc);\nout1 = vec(hn, 0, 0, 1);\n",
									"fontface": 0,
									"fontname": "<Monospaced>",
									"fontsize": 12.0,
									"id": "gen-obj-2",
