							{
								"box": {
									"code": "// codebox_pass.gen -- f_ks stage 0b: holds last frame's state u, or reseeds it. 256x256 float32.\n// Mirror: tests/modules/ks/ks_mirror.seed_state() (seeding); identity otherwise.\n//\n// Inputs: the first inlet is the `r draw` bang (unused; it only triggers the render every frame, and the\n// feedback arrives on a cold inlet so it cannot retrigger the loop), the second is the feedback state\n// (R = u, from the nl stage through the hold stage), the third is the noise texture (R in [0,1), from\n// the seed stage).\n// reseed = 1 replaces the state with (2*noise - 1) * amp: uniform in [-amp, amp], never zero (u = 0 is a\n// fixed point, FR-003). reseed fires on load and on the reset trigger (FR-007).\n//   - SELF-HEAL: a texel of the feedback that is exactly 0 is reseeded from the noise too. A live KS\n//     field never holds an exact 0 (float32 values), so this fires only when the state was lost: a\n//     fresh module, a GL context rebuilt by a window mode change (floating <-> fullscreen), or a\n//     non-finite texel the nl stage zapped to 0. u = 0 everywhere is a fixed point, so without this a\n//     lost state stays flat grey forever\n//   - selection uses switch(), not mix(): mix(NaN, x, 1) is still NaN, so a poisoned feedback\n//     texel could survive a reseed through mix\n//   - the feedback is NaN/Inf-guarded: abs(x) < 1e30 (NaN == NaN is TRUE on this GPU)\nParam reseed(0);\nParam amp(1);\n\nfb = nearest(in2, norm).x;\nfb = switch(abs(fb) < 1e30, fb, 0);\nnz = (nearest(in3, norm).x * 2 - 1) * amp;\nkept = switch(fb == 0, nz, fb);\nout1 = vec(switch(reseed >= 0.5, nz, kept), 0, 0, 1);\n",
									"fontface": 0,
									"fontname": "<Monospaced>",
