							{
								"box": {
									"code": "// codebox_nl.gen -- f_ks stage 6: the real-space nonlinearity, on the linear-step result.\n// u_new = u_lin - dt * 0.5 * |grad u_lin|^2 with periodic central differences. 256x256 float32.\n// Mirror: tests/modules/ks/ks_mirror.nonlinear_step().\n//\n// Input in1 = u_lin (R, from the ix stage). Output R = u_new, A = 1: this is the solver state and\n// the feedback edge (nl -> pass).\n//   - neighbors are read with integer indices wrapped by wrap() and normalized texel-centre\n//     coordinates: the domain is periodic and nothing relies on sampler wrap behavior\n//   - dx = L / N, so 1 / dx = N / L\n//   - containment: a non-finite or huge result is zapped / clamped here, so the feedback loop can\n//     never carry NaN/Inf (FR-008). The clamp (+-100) is far above the measured |u| (15 to 20 at\n//     the dt ceiling) and is inactive in normal running; it is a backstop, modeled in the mirror\nParam dt(0.05);\nParam L(50);\n\nN = 256;\nbx = floor(norm.x * N);\nby = floor(norm.y * N);\nxp = (wrap(bx + 1, 0, N) + 0.5) / N;\nxm = (wrap(bx - 1, 0, N) + 0.5) / N;\nyp = (wrap(by + 1, 0, N) + 0.5) / N;\nym = (wrap(by - 1, 0, N) + 0.5) / N;\ninv_dx = N / L;\ngx = (nearest(in1, vec(xp, norm.y)).x - nearest(in1, vec(xm, norm.y)).x) * (0.5 * inv_dx);\ngy = (nearest(in1, vec(norm.x, yp)).x - nearest(in1, vec(norm.x, ym)).x) * (0.5 * inv_dx);\nq = gx * gx + gy * gy;\nun = nearest(in1, norm).x - dt * 0.5 * q;\nun = switch(abs(un) < 1e30, un, 0);\nun = clamp(un, -100, 100);\n\nout1 = vec(un, 0, 0, 1);\n",
